is
> off Earth's equatorial axis by ~5=B0.

Lojgugde would be in the Earth's shadow as often as the Moon is eclipsed,=
=20
which is about twice a year, and in the Moon's shadow as often as an eclips=
e=20
of the Sun passes through the middle of the Earth, which is somewhat less=
=20
often. (There may be five solar eclipses in a year, but they pass over=20
different parts of the Earth.) Both occur when the Sun passes through the=
=20
plane of the Moon's orbit. L4 is eclipsed by the Moon 1/6 through a lunatio=
n=20
(starting at the dark, not new, moon) and by the Earth 1/3 through a=20
lunation. L5 is eclipsed by the Earth 2/3 through a lunation and by the Moo=
n=20
5/6 through a lunation.

